        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8380/3 Endometrioid adenocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63180,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C74.0 &amp; XH0SD2 Adenocarcinoma of fallopian tube &amp; Endometrioid adenocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63181,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> endometrioid adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63182,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63183,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fallopian tube</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63184,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid carcinoma of the fallopian tube can present with a pelvic mass or abdominal pain, or it can be an incidental finding, mostly in the distal two&nbsp;thirds of the fallopian tube {8946874}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63185,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid carcinoma is the second most common type of tubal carcinoma. Endometrial sampling should exclude synchronous or metastatic carcinoma {31097111}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63186,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63187,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Type&nbsp;II stem cell outgrowths can be associated with endometrial endometrioid carcinomas, &beta;-catenin&ndash;positive&nbsp;tubal endometrioid intraepithelial neoplasia&nbsp;/ atypical hyperplasia, and &beta;-catenin&ndash;positive&nbsp;endometrioid tubal carcinomas; this is similar to endometrial endometrioid carcinomas {31574529}, suggesting a possible carcinogenic sequence.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-01T14:30:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63188,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid carcinoma is a yellow friable mass causing tubal dilatation, ranging from 0.4 to 6&nbsp;cm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63189,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The morphology is similar to that of endometrial endometrioid carcinomas (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/223\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Endometrioid carcinoma of the uterine corpus</em>). Endometrioid carcinomas of the fallopian tube often show areas of solid growth, spindled cells, and small glands that may resemble female adnexal tumours of probable Wolffian origin {8946874}. On rare occasions, they may have a prominent spindle cell appearance with squamous-like differentiation or osseous metaplasia, leading to confusion with carcinosarcoma {24901398}. Unlike serous carcinomas, endometrioid carcinomas are WT1-negative and usually p53-wildtype. The differential diagnosis includes mainly metastatic endometrioid carcinoma, including spread from an ovarian endometrioid tumour, microscopic extraovarian sex cord proliferations, and female adnexal tumour of probable Wolffian origin {31097111}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T08:06:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63190,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Malignant cells may be identified in pelvic washings in advanced cases {24368120; 31734259}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63191,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63192,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tubal mural proliferation of closely packed endometrioid glands with or without squamous metaplasia; in low-grade tumours, endometrioid differentiation can be diagnosed on H&amp;E-stained specimens.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> diffuse high-grade atypia out of proportion to architectural features raises serous carcinoma as a possibility; WT1 negativity; wildtype p53; normal endometrium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63193,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>This entity is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:46:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63194,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognosis depends on stage. Most cases present at a low stage, do not invade the fimbria, and have a favourable prognosis {31097111}. Location in the fimbria and/or deep invasion are adverse prognostic features {23195378; 24901398}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:32:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]